course: dictionary
lesson: 1802
title: Two meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues around the word show you which meaning the writer wants. «Ice or frozen peas should be wrapped in a cloth and used for about 15 to 20 minutes at a time.» Wrapped and ice tell you that a cloth is a piece of material used for covering.
explain: Cloth can also mean the material itself, the stuff that clothes and curtains are made from. A clue for this is an adjective, such as soft or blue. «Her new dress was made from soft blue cloth.» Here the cloth is the material, not one piece of it.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Press with a clean cloth to stop bleeding» still makes sense with a piece of material for cleaning or covering. If your meaning does not fit, look again at the clues.
fact: Cloth is material made by weaving or knitting threads.
fact: A cloth is a piece of material used for cleaning or covering, like a dishcloth or a tablecloth.
fact: Cloth as material is uncountable, so you say «some cloth», not «a cloth» for the material.
fact: «Cloth» can mean a piece for cleaning, as in «wipe the table with a cloth».
exercise: «Wipe the table with a cloth after you eat.» What is a cloth in this sentence? | Material for making a warm winter coat | *A piece of material for cleaning | A kind of table | Thread for sewing buttons on
exercise: Mum says, «press with a clean cloth to stop bleeding». Find and copy the word that names the thing used to press the cut. | plaster | bleeding | *cloth | clean
exercise: «Her new dress was made from soft blue cloth.» What kind of cloth is it? | *Material for making clothes | A piece for wiping up spills | A bandage for a cut | A rag for dusting
test: «The tablecloth was covered in jam.» What does tablecloth mean? | Cloth for making tables | *A piece of material covering a table | A bowl for soup | Plate of food
test: «Ice should be wrapped in a cloth, because ice on bare skin can burn.» Why is the ice wrapped in a cloth? | To wash the ice clean | To make the ice taste nicer | To make the ice melt faster | *So it does not touch bare skin directly
exam: Which sentence uses cloth to mean a piece of material for covering? | «Cloth can be woven or knitted.» | «Mum bought two metres of cloth for the curtains.» | *«Cover the bread with a clean cloth.» | «The cloth is made of cotton and wool.»
